SPLIT LICENSING
---------------
Everything in this repository is Apache-2.0 EXCEPT the `host/` directory,
which is licensed under the GNU General Public License v3.0 or later
(see host/LICENSE). `host/` holds the Linux companion software — offline
analysis of recorded takes and the Praat golden-file generator — which
imports Praat/parselmouth (GPLv3) in-process. No code crosses the `host/`
boundary in either direction: firmware never depends on `host/`, and
`host/` is never linked into firmware. The two halves communicate only
through files on disk whose formats are specified under `protocols/specs/`.
See docs/adr/0004-split-licensing.md (pre-registered in docs/adr/README.md).

Consequently, on the firmware side only MIT-, BSD- and Apache-2.0-licensed
components may appear in `idf_component.yml` or on the link line. GPL, AGPL
and LGPL code, and code under field-of-use licences (the "Espressif MIT"
licence of ESP-ADF/ESP-SR), is studied as read-only reference and never
copied. Every source file carries `SPDX-FileCopyrightText` and
`SPDX-License-Identifier` headers.

